      <h1>Bitcoin Ecosystem</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Understand the people, companies, markets, and communities that build around Bitcoin without treating any business, personality, repository, event, or institution as a source of protocol authority. This category maps influence, incentives, custody, dependencies, tradeoffs, and evidence across sixteen canonical guides.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>4 subcategories</li><li>16 guides</li><li>Ecosystem map</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-31</li></ul>
      <p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Preview only. Guide cards and navigation remain inactive because published destinations and confirmed URLs do not exist.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="msc-learn-subcategories" aria-label="Bitcoin Ecosystem guide preview">
      <section class="msc-learn-subcategory" data-msc-subcategory="People"><h2>People</h2><div class="msc-learn-card-grid">
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-065" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-065</p><h3>Who Builds on Bitcoin?</h3><p>Map the overlapping roles that contribute to Bitcoin-related protocol research, software, products, infrastructure, education, policy, media, design, and culture without inventing a central builder organization.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>21 to 25 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-066" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-066</p><h3>What Bitcoin Developers Do</h3><p>Follow development from research and issue definition through implementation, review, testing, release, deployment, security response, documentation, and maintenance while keeping every permission scoped to a specific project.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>22 to 26 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-067" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-067</p><h3>Bitcoin Artists and the Culture They Shape</h3><p>Explore how artists, designers, writers, filmmakers, musicians, archivists, and communities create symbols, criticism, interfaces, and historical memory while culture, popularity, price, intellectual property, and consensus remain separate.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>22 to 26 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-068" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-068</p><h3>How Bitcoin Industry Leaders Shape the Ecosystem</h3><p>Evaluate practical influence through capital, products, infrastructure, funding, distribution, policy access, and media reach by tracing incentives, accountability, concentration, exit options, and the limits of organizational power.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>23 to 27 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
      </div></section>

      <section class="msc-learn-subcategory" data-msc-subcategory="Companies"><h2>Companies</h2><div class="msc-learn-card-grid">
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-069" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-069</p><h3>How Public Companies Participate in Bitcoin</h3><p>Separate treasury holdings, mining, custody, market services, payment products, financial wrappers, accounting, financing, and shareholder exposure so corporate participation is not mistaken for direct bitcoin ownership or protocol governance.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>18 to 22 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-070" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-070</p><h3>How Bitcoin Startups Build and Compete</h3><p>Assess young Bitcoin businesses through the problem they solve, product layer, custody model, revenue, unit economics, funding, distribution, security practice, vendor dependencies, portability, and failure plan rather than attention alone.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>18 to 22 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-071" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-071</p><h3>How Bitcoin Mining Companies Operate</h3><p>Connect power, sites, cooling, ASIC fleets, firmware, pools, labor, capital, hashrate, difficulty, fees, and treasury decisions while keeping mining companies distinct from pools, manufacturers, and validating nodes.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>20 to 24 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-072" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-072</p><h3>What Bitcoin Infrastructure Companies Do</h3><p>Identify the functional dependencies created by hosted nodes, APIs, indexers, Lightning systems, mining tools, signing interfaces, data services, security operations, and enterprise integrations, including privacy, availability, and migration risk.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>19 to 23 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
      </div></section>

      <section class="msc-learn-subcategory" data-msc-subcategory="Markets"><h2>Markets</h2><div class="msc-learn-card-grid">
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-073" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-073</p><h3>How Bitcoin Exchanges Work</h3><p>Trace the complete path from on-chain deposit detection and confirmation policy through internal credit, order matching, custody, withdrawal review, signing, broadcast, and settlement so an exchange account is not confused with key control.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Guide</li><li>9 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-074" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-074</p><h3>How Bitcoin Wallet Providers Operate</h3><p>Map which provider supplies the interface, signer, device, server, node, recovery process, coordinator, or custody service, then ask who can authorize spending, observe activity, preserve recovery data, and continue after provider loss.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Guide</li><li>9 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-075" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-075</p><h3>How Bitcoin Marketplaces Work</h3><p>Follow listings, discovery, agreement, payment conditions, escrow or coordination, settlement, delivery, reputation, and disputes while keeping Bitcoin transaction validity separate from off-chain promises and legal outcomes.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>10 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-076" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-076</p><h3>What Bitcoin Service Providers Do</h3><p>Define the exact outsourced function, credentials, data access, custody, fees, legal entity, dependencies, verification options, continuity plan, and exit path behind payment, infrastructure, data, compliance, conversion, or support services.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>9 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
      </div></section>

      <section class="msc-learn-subcategory" data-msc-subcategory="Community"><h2>Community</h2><div class="msc-learn-card-grid">
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-077" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-077</p><h3>Why Bitcoin Conferences Matter</h3><p>Examine how organizers, sponsors, speakers, workshops, technical sessions, media, business meetings, art, and regional participation can create learning and collaboration while an agenda never becomes an official Bitcoin roadmap.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>9 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-078" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-078</p><h3>How Bitcoin Communities Form and Grow</h3><p>Study recurring communities through shared practice, newcomer pathways, useful work, local context, funding, moderation, safety, disagreement, and capture risk rather than treating audience size as durable adoption.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>8 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-079" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-079</p><h3>Major Milestones in Bitcoin History</h3><p>Use a dated timeline to separate proposals, implementations, releases, activations, business failures, legal changes, cultural events, and measured adoption without ranking history by market price.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Surface</li><li>History</li><li>10 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
        <article class="msc-learn-guide-card" data-msc-guide-id="MSC-GUIDE-080" aria-disabled="true"><p class="msc-section-kicker">MSC-GUIDE-080</p><h3>How Bitcoin Open-Source Projects Work</h3><p>Understand how licenses, repositories, contributors, reviewers, maintainers, releases, funding, forks, security reporting, dependencies, and long-term maintenance shape a project without creating authority over Bitcoin consensus.</p><ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>12 minutes</li></ul><p class="msc-learn-preview-note">Read guide remains inactive until publication and URL confirmation.</p></article>
      </div></section>
